# Local operator tooling — NOT source, NOT for git.
#
# Why this entry exists (2026-08-13, architect): `tools/` was untracked but
# unignored, which is indistinguishable from "staged for the next commit" to
# `git add -A`. Two separate payloads were one careless command from entering
# history:
#   1. tools/pdf-content-ingestor/.env.staging.local — holds a Supabase
#      SERVICE_ROLE key. (Line 70's `.env*` rule already matched this file, so
#      it was covered; this entry is defence in depth, not the primary control.
#      Key ROTATION is a Supabase-dashboard action and is handled separately —
#      ignoring the file does not un-expose a key that already leaked.)
#   2. tools/pdf-content-ingestor/data/assets/ — extracted page images for 49
#      PDFs. Large binary payload, regenerable from source PDFs, never source.
# The directory is deliberately NOT deleted: the operator may still want to
# inspect/run it locally.
tools/

# Local Python virtualenv for BGE embedding experiments (regenerable)
.venv-bge/
graphify-out/

# Local `npm run build` output captured to a file for debugging — not source.
# Found untracked at apps/host/build.log during the 2026-08-23 uncommitted-work
# triage; add a repo-wide pattern so it can't recur silently in any workspace.
build.log

# Root-level Vitest report blobs (large per-run JSON artifacts, e.g.
# blob-2-4.json was 15 MB). The existing apps/host/.vitest-reports/ entry above
# only covers that app-scoped path — this repo-root variant was found
# untracked separately during the same triage and needs its own entry.
.vitest-reports/
